    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Aug 15, 2024, at 2:47 PM, Mihajlo Milic &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mihajlo....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello everyone,<div>I have a shape dataset for 2504 individuals classified in one of 243 species. So each species has more than one individual and the number of individuals per species is unequal. Do you know how to calculate mean shapes for each species? I know this is more a general R question than a geomorph, but I believe someone had experience with this.<br></div><div>Mihajlo</div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-r-pack...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/CAJy6d1T%2Ba%2ByzCRfRhopnJHFHozgWun%3D-jE7tWVm2jJarVqSaxA%40mail.gmail.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/CAJy6d1T%252Ba%252ByzCRfRhopnJHFHozgWun%253D-jE7tWVm2jJarVqSaxA%2540mail.gmail.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483327436000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0oXUQqjllEabCQwS4bveDT\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/CAJy6d1T%2Ba%2ByzCRfRhopnJHFHozgWun%3D-jE7tWVm2jJarVqSaxA%40mail.gmail.com</a>.<br>\r\n</div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ]
